{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1053549-wood-dragon-claws-adjustments-to-the-spell","id":1053549,"title":"Wood Dragon Claws & adjustments to the spell?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-22T18:06:54-08:00","id":1053549,"title":"Wood Dragon Claws & adjustments to the spell?","content":"Hello all, I was wondering how you all feel about having WDC summon a melee weapon instead, as this seems like a method to have more individuality to the spell and remove the issues of it combining with Black Claw Style?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T04:10:09-08:00","id":1053748,"title":"","content":"What issues does it have combining with Black Claw Style? The devs have already explicitly said that it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T12:52:16-08:00","id":1053962,"title":"","content":"Somebody wanted to &quot;borrow&quot; Spring Razor's Evocations for WDC, and combo that with Black Claw for ridiculous stacked poison damage.<br /> <br /> I can accept that this might be broken, but I fail to see how this has now become a problem with WDC. Sounds like throwing out the baby with the bathwater to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T14:11:24-08:00","id":1054001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1053549-wood-dragon-claws-adjustments-to-the-spell#post1053549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello all, I was wondering how you all feel about having WDC summon a melee weapon instead, as this seems like a method to have more individuality to the spell and remove the issues of it combining with Black Claw Style?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to make a spell that summons a weapon, I suppose Wood Dragon Claw is a decent baseline to compare it to. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't see the issue with allowing it to combine with Black Claw Style (or any other Martial Art style for that matter). In fact, I'm not sure what kind of problem there could be, provided you don't do something silly like allow your player to create questionable Evocations that could cause problems when combined with various Martial Arts styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T14:39:28-08:00","id":1054020,"title":"","content":"Yeah that complaint still puzzles me.<br /> <br /> I mean, I personally think that the opinion is wrong and that WDC is not actually BCS compatible, but let's ignore that for a moment (because it's beside the point). If the worry is that BCS goes nuts when you stack multiple poison sources, then it's the <i>Style </i>that is the problem. After all, other poison sources aren't hard to think of even if you take WDC/Spring Razor nonsense out of the conversation. Looking at this scenario and concluding that the problem is WDC seems odd to me. Like watching someone getting ready to torch a house with a flamethrower and thinking &quot;Gee, someone should take his <i>matches </i>away from him.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T14:59:38-08:00","id":1054033,"title":"","content":"Vance and Holden have both said that BC and WDC can be used together.<br /> <br /> I find the puzzling part is that because of a third, unrelated thing which you can hypothetically allow is the actual thing that makes all of this a problem. Like, you can say, &quot;No, you can't use those Evocations from Spring Razor for your WDC, those are Spring Razor's evocations.&quot; nevermind the million other reasons you can explicitly block this triple combo.<br /> <br /> It's a &quot;Mother, May I?&quot; problem born entirely out of a hypothetical scenario that you can crush before it's even a problem and never enter &quot;house rule&quot; territory to begin with.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To go back to the original question, I don't think anyone will kill you if you make &quot;Wood Dragon's Fang&quot; and make it give you a sword that is rooted to one or both of your hands or whatever. That could be cool. I would <i>not </i>make this change specifically to invalidate its use with BCS. If that part is the actual problem, just tell that player they can't or ask them not to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 02-23-2017, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T15:16:39-08:00","id":1054043,"title":"","content":"Honestly, my main issue with combining WDC and Black Claw is that Black Claw is a style about being harmless, adorable, and fragile and I feel like having giant wooden paws with foot long thorns coming out the ends undermines that aesthetic to a significant degree. Plus the style says unarmed only.<br /> <br /> Coming back to the point however, I used WDC as the basis for a spell that creates a pellet crossbow out of sandstone, so I'm totally of the opinion that you can use it as the basis for all kinds of &quot;summon an artifact weapon&quot; spells.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T10:10:01-08:00","id":1054364,"title":"","content":"My main objection to WDC/Black Claw compatibility isn't the Spring Razor / Black Claw thing specifically (I chalk that up to a lack of clarity in the rules for stacking poisons more than anything), or even really anything to do with Black Claw at all. It's the general idea that WDC counts as &quot;unarmed&quot; but gives you artifact weapon stats and access to evocations, and that feels like a no-brainer purchase for anyone using an unarmed-only Style like Black Claw or blending two or more Styles whose common weapon is &quot;unarmed&quot; (who otherwise can't have those things)<br /> <br /> I guess it just feels like Sorcery is a weird place to hide a readily-accessible button that undoes one of the main weaknesses of Martial Arts. Unless you're looking for a Doctor Strange-like feel where the line between Martial Artist and Sorcerer is vague at best, and every Martial Artist knows enough Sorcery to be able to summon a personal custom magic weapon that complements their fighting style, and (bonus) perform Workings. Don't get me wrong, I think that's actually a pretty compelling setup (especially for Sidereals, if they can afford the motes for WDC) but generally in Exalted, Sorcerer and Martial Artist are treated as two separate (XP-sinky) paths.<br /> <br /> Back to the OP, I think treating WDC as Razor Claws and/or Smashfist would make more sense than Melee but have basically the same effect. It's not compatibility with Styles that's a problem, it's being compatible with <i>every</i> unarmed Style. And as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar226_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"226\" data-vbnamecard=\"226\">BrilliantRain</a> says it's a fine template for whatever other custom weapon-spell (Melee or otherwise) you might want to create.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 02-24-2017, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T10:31:26-08:00","id":1054368,"title":"","content":"WDC works for Tiger Style and Black Claw. It doesn't work for every other style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T10:40:37-08:00","id":1054371,"title":"","content":"WDC doesn't exactly count as unarmed as written. Per the writeup, it's compatible with &quot;Martial Arts that use claw-type weapons or rending strikes, such as Tiger Style.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}